{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "34e9c0f7",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "34e9c0f7"
      },
      "source": [
        "# Transport in Europe: Motorisation and Emissions\n",
        "\n",
        "Question 1: What explains how many cars a country has per inhabitant?\n",
        "\n",
        "Question 2: What explains the transport emissions per capita?\n",
        "\n",
        "The data come from Eurostat. We use one model for each question."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "fee1ee7b",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "fee1ee7b"
      },
      "source": [
        "## 1. Setup"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "fb2d21be",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "fb2d21be"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "!pip install eurostat"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "28c7bf7f",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "28c7bf7f"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "import eurostat\n",
        "import pandas as pd\n",
        "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
        "import seaborn as sns\n",
        "import statsmodels.api as sm\n",
        "import statsmodels.stats.diagnostic as smd\n",
        "from statsmodels.stats.outliers_influence import variance_inflation_factor\n",
        "from statsmodels.stats.stattools import durbin_watson\n",
        "from scipy import stats"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "1f973bdb",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "1f973bdb"
      },
      "source": [
        "## 2. Configuration\n",
        "\n",
        "The dataset codes and the filter values. Some Eurostat tables contain more than\n",
        "one unit, so we have to pick one."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "8adea7c0",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "8adea7c0"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "CARS_CODE = \"road_eqs_carhab\"       # cars per 1000 inhabitants\n",
        "GDP_CODE = \"sdg_08_10\"              # GDP per capita\n",
        "DENSITY_CODE = \"tps00003\"           # population density\n",
        "POP_CODE = \"tps00001\"               # population\n",
        "AGE_CODE = \"road_eqs_carage\"        # cars by age\n",
        "EMISSION_CODE = \"env_air_gge\"       # greenhouse gases by sector\n",
        "\n",
        "GDP_UNIT = \"CLV20_EUR_HAB\"          # euro per capita, not the growth rate\n",
        "AGE_UNIT = \"NR\"                     # number of cars\n",
        "AGE_10_TO_20 = \"Y10-20\"             # cars 10 to 20 years old\n",
        "AGE_ABOVE_20 = \"Y_GT20\"             # cars older than 20 years\n",
        "AIRPOL = \"GHG\"                      # greenhouse gases\n",
        "SECTOR = \"CRF1A3\"                   # transport\n",
        "EMISSION_UNIT = \"THS_T\"             # thousand tonnes\n",
        "\n",
        "START_YEAR = 2010"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "64e61096",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "64e61096"
      },
      "source": [
        "## 3. Loading the data\n",
        "\n",
        "Eurostat gives one column per year. We need one row per country and year, so we\n",
        "rebuild the table with two loops. We also keep only the two-letter country\n",
        "codes, because EU27_2020 and EA19 are groups of countries, not countries."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "0f2c787a",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "0f2c787a"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "class EurostatLoader:\n",
        "\n",
        "    def __init__(self, start_year):\n",
        "        self.start_year = start_year\n",
        "\n",
        "    def load(self, dataset_code):\n",
        "        return eurostat.get_data_df(dataset_code)\n",
        "\n",
        "    def to_long(self, raw, value_name):\n",
        "        year_columns = []\n",
        "        for column in raw.columns:\n",
        "            if str(column).isdigit():\n",
        "                year_columns.append(column)\n",
        "\n",
        "        countries = list(raw[\"geo\\\\TIME_PERIOD\"])\n",
        "\n",
        "        country_list = []\n",
        "        year_list = []\n",
        "        value_list = []\n",
        "\n",
        "        for year in year_columns:\n",
        "            if int(year) >= self.start_year:\n",
        "                values = list(raw[year])\n",
        "                for i in range(len(countries)):\n",
        "                    if len(countries[i]) == 2:\n",
        "                        country_list.append(countries[i])\n",
        "                        year_list.append(int(year))\n",
        "                        value_list.append(values[i])\n",
        "\n",
        "        long = pd.DataFrame({\"country\": country_list,\n",
        "                             \"year\": year_list,\n",
        "                             value_name: value_list})\n",
        "        return long.dropna()\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "loader = EurostatLoader(START_YEAR)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "b67b6cf1",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "b67b6cf1"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "raw_cars = loader.load(CARS_CODE)\n",
        "raw_gdp = loader.load(GDP_CODE)\n",
        "raw_density = loader.load(DENSITY_CODE)\n",
        "raw_pop = loader.load(POP_CODE)\n",
        "raw_age = loader.load(AGE_CODE)\n",
        "raw_emission = loader.load(EMISSION_CODE)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"loaded\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "2fdc2425",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "2fdc2425"
      },
      "source": [
        "### 3.1 The main variables\n",
        "\n",
        "We count the rows per country and year. The maximum has to be 1. A higher\n",
        "number means a filter is missing."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "7330978f",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "7330978f"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "gdp_data = raw_gdp[raw_gdp[\"unit\"] == GDP_UNIT]\n",
        "\n",
        "cars = loader.to_long(raw_cars, \"cars_per_1000\")\n",
        "gdp = loader.to_long(gdp_data, \"gdp_pc\")\n",
        "density = loader.to_long(raw_density, \"density\")\n",
        "population = loader.to_long(raw_pop, \"population\")\n",
        "\n",
        "panel = cars.merge(gdp, on=[\"country\", \"year\"])\n",
        "panel = panel.merge(density, on=[\"country\", \"year\"])\n",
        "panel = panel.merge(population, on=[\"country\", \"year\"])\n",
        "\n",
        "check = panel.groupby([\"country\", \"year\"], as_index=False)[\"gdp_pc\"].count()\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Rows:\", panel.shape[0])\n",
        "print(\"Countries:\", len(panel[\"country\"].unique()))\n",
        "print(\"Rows per country and year, maximum:\", check[\"gdp_pc\"].max())\n",
        "panel.head()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "91319847",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "91319847"
      },
      "source": [
        "### 3.2 Age of the car fleet\n",
        "\n",
        "We load the two oldest age classes and the total, then compute the share of\n",
        "cars older than ten years."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "e4b6fcf5",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "e4b6fcf5"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "age_data = raw_age[raw_age[\"unit\"] == AGE_UNIT]\n",
        "\n",
        "old_10_to_20 = loader.to_long(age_data[age_data[\"age\"] == AGE_10_TO_20], \"old_10_to_20\")\n",
        "old_above_20 = loader.to_long(age_data[age_data[\"age\"] == AGE_ABOVE_20], \"old_above_20\")\n",
        "all_cars = loader.to_long(age_data[age_data[\"age\"] == \"TOTAL\"], \"total\")\n",
        "\n",
        "fleet = old_10_to_20.merge(old_above_20, on=[\"country\", \"year\"])\n",
        "fleet = fleet.merge(all_cars, on=[\"country\", \"year\"])\n",
        "\n",
        "fleet[\"old_cars_share\"] = (fleet[\"old_10_to_20\"] + fleet[\"old_above_20\"]) / fleet[\"total\"] * 100\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Rows:\", fleet.shape[0])\n",
        "fleet.head()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "8a0d0efb",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "8a0d0efb"
      },
      "source": [
        "### 3.3 Emissions\n",
        "\n",
        "We keep the greenhouse gases from transport in thousand tonnes and divide them\n",
        "by the population. That gives tonnes per inhabitant."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "3f7e2c5a",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "3f7e2c5a"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "emission_data = raw_emission[raw_emission[\"airpol\"] == AIRPOL]\n",
        "emission_data = emission_data[emission_data[\"src_crf\"] == SECTOR]\n",
        "emission_data = emission_data[emission_data[\"unit\"] == EMISSION_UNIT]\n",
        "\n",
        "emissions = loader.to_long(emission_data, \"emission_total\")\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Rows:\", emissions.shape[0])\n",
        "emissions.head()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "97049790",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "97049790"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "panel = panel.merge(emissions, on=[\"country\", \"year\"])\n",
        "panel[\"emission_pc\"] = panel[\"emission_total\"] * 1000 / panel[\"population\"]\n",
        "\n",
        "panel = panel.merge(fleet, on=[\"country\", \"year\"])\n",
        "panel = panel.dropna()\n",
        "\n",
        "check = panel.groupby([\"country\", \"year\"], as_index=False)[\"gdp_pc\"].count()\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Rows:\", panel.shape[0])\n",
        "print(\"Countries:\", len(panel[\"country\"].unique()))\n",
        "print(\"Rows per country and year, maximum:\", check[\"gdp_pc\"].max())\n",
        "panel.head()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "983e926a",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "983e926a"
      },
      "source": [
        "## 4. Descriptive statistics"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "45be2444",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "45be2444"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "panel[[\"cars_per_1000\", \"gdp_pc\", \"density\", \"emission_pc\", \"old_cars_share\"]].describe()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "8f9c605b",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "8f9c605b"
      },
      "source": [
        "We use only the last year. In a panel the same country would appear many\n",
        "times, and the observations would not be independent."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "4082d532",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "4082d532"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "latest_year = panel[\"year\"].max()\n",
        "data = panel[panel[\"year\"] == latest_year]\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Year:\", latest_year)\n",
        "print(\"Countries:\", data.shape[0])\n",
        "data.sort_values(\"emission_pc\", ascending=False).head(5)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "78c9e305",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "78c9e305"
      },
      "source": [
        "## 5. Charts"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "53ddac9e",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "53ddac9e"
      },
      "source": [
        "### 5.1 Emissions over time\n",
        "\n",
        "The average over all countries. Each country counts the same."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "3130cf44",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "3130cf44"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "yearly = panel.groupby(\"year\", as_index=False)[\"emission_pc\"].mean()\n",
        "\n",
        "fig, ax = plt.subplots()\n",
        "ax.plot(yearly[\"year\"], yearly[\"emission_pc\"])\n",
        "ax.set_xlabel(\"Year\")\n",
        "ax.set_ylabel(\"Tonnes per inhabitant\")\n",
        "ax.set_title(\"Transport emissions per capita\")\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "9b5632cd",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "9b5632cd"
      },
      "source": [
        "### 5.2 The countries compared\n",
        "\n",
        "This chart shows why we drop Luxembourg later."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "a258bf2e",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "a258bf2e"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "ranked = data.sort_values(\"emission_pc\", ascending=False)\n",
        "\n",
        "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(10, 5))\n",
        "ax.bar(ranked[\"country\"], ranked[\"emission_pc\"])\n",
        "ax.set_xlabel(\"Country\")\n",
        "ax.set_ylabel(\"Tonnes per inhabitant\")\n",
        "ax.set_title(\"Transport emissions per capita\")\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "e4638f6c",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "e4638f6c"
      },
      "source": [
        "### 5.3 Cars and emissions"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "713e212f",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "713e212f"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "fig, ax = plt.subplots()\n",
        "ax.scatter(data[\"cars_per_1000\"], data[\"emission_pc\"])\n",
        "ax.set_xlabel(\"Cars per 1000 inhabitants\")\n",
        "ax.set_ylabel(\"Tonnes per inhabitant\")\n",
        "ax.set_title(\"Cars and emissions\")\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "ae73404e",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "ae73404e"
      },
      "source": [
        "### 5.4 Correlations"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "169e07a6",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "169e07a6"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "corr = data[[\"cars_per_1000\", \"gdp_pc\", \"density\", \"emission_pc\", \"old_cars_share\"]].corr()\n",
        "\n",
        "fig, ax = plt.subplots()\n",
        "sns.heatmap(corr, annot=True, cmap=\"coolwarm\", ax=ax)\n",
        "ax.set_title(\"Correlation matrix\")\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "5.5 Age of the car fleet by country\n",
        "\n",
        "The share of each age class in the car fleet. This is what the variable old_cars_share summarises.\n"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "n-eAAGbPzfyT"
      },
      "id": "n-eAAGbPzfyT"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "AGE_CLASSES = [\"Y_LT2\", \"Y2-5\", \"Y5-10\", \"Y10-20\", \"Y_GT20\"]\n",
        "\n",
        "shares = all_cars\n",
        "for age_class in AGE_CLASSES:\n",
        "    part = loader.to_long(age_data[age_data[\"age\"] == age_class], age_class)\n",
        "    shares = shares.merge(part, on=[\"country\", \"year\"])\n",
        "\n",
        "shares = shares[shares[\"year\"] == latest_year]\n",
        "\n",
        "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(10, 5))\n",
        "\n",
        "bottom = 0\n",
        "for age_class in AGE_CLASSES:\n",
        "    share = shares[age_class] / shares[\"total\"] * 100\n",
        "    ax.bar(shares[\"country\"], share, bottom=bottom, label=age_class)\n",
        "    bottom = bottom + share\n",
        "\n",
        "ax.set_xlabel(\"Country\")\n",
        "ax.set_ylabel(\"Share of the fleet in percent\")\n",
        "ax.set_title(\"Age of the car fleet\")\n",
        "ax.legend()\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "RkU24jpNzi4-"
      },
      "id": "RkU24jpNzi4-",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "75e39fea",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "75e39fea"
      },
      "source": [
        "## 6. The sample\n",
        "\n",
        "We drop Luxembourg. The country sells fuel to drivers from its neighbours, and\n",
        "its GDP per capita includes people who work there but live abroad. Both\n",
        "variables of our model are too high because of this. Chart 5.2 shows the\n",
        "distance to the next country.\n",
        "\n",
        "We also build the square of GDP. It goes into model 1 because the relation\n",
        "gets flatter: at some point a household has enough cars."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "DcDl-pOBzeL8"
      },
      "id": "DcDl-pOBzeL8",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "7f197f3e",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "7f197f3e"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "data = data.copy()\n",
        "data[\"gdp_pc2\"] = data[\"gdp_pc\"] ** 2\n",
        "\n",
        "no_lu = data[data[\"country\"] != \"LU\"]\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Observations:\", no_lu.shape[0])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "8aa35c90",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "8aa35c90"
      },
      "source": [
        "## 7. Model 1: cars\n",
        "\n",
        "`cars_per_1000 = b0 + b1 gdp_pc + b2 gdp_pc^2 + b3 density + b4 old_cars_share + u`"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "5ff2f0ba",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "5ff2f0ba"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "x_cars = sm.add_constant(no_lu[[\"gdp_pc\", \"gdp_pc2\", \"density\", \"old_cars_share\"]])\n",
        "model_cars = sm.OLS(no_lu[\"cars_per_1000\"], x_cars).fit()\n",
        "\n",
        "print(model_cars.summary())"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "c5cba886",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "c5cba886"
      },
      "source": [
        "### 7.1 Turning point\n",
        "\n",
        "For a quadratic relation the top of the curve is at -b / (2a). Above this\n",
        "income more money does not bring more cars."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "fc41a994",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "fc41a994"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "b = model_cars.params[\"gdp_pc\"]\n",
        "a = model_cars.params[\"gdp_pc2\"]\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Turning point at\", round(-b / (2 * a), 0), \"euro\")\n",
        "print(\"Highest GDP in the sample:\", round(no_lu[\"gdp_pc\"].max(), 0), \"euro\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "d193d267",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "d193d267"
      },
      "source": [
        "## 8. Model 2: emissions\n",
        "\n",
        "`emission_pc = b0 + b1 cars_per_1000 + b2 gdp_pc + b3 density + b4 old_cars_share + u`\n",
        "\n",
        "Here GDP is linear. The flattening in model 1 is about the number of cars, not\n",
        "about the emissions of one car."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "b29bb6d7",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "b29bb6d7"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "x_emission = sm.add_constant(no_lu[[\"cars_per_1000\", \"gdp_pc\", \"density\", \"old_cars_share\"]])\n",
        "model_emission = sm.OLS(no_lu[\"emission_pc\"], x_emission).fit()\n",
        "\n",
        "print(model_emission.summary())"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "885463f4",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "885463f4"
      },
      "source": [
        "### 8.1 Cars and emissions with a regression line"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 42,
      "id": "aae3fc06",
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/",
          "height": 472
        },
        "id": "aae3fc06",
        "outputId": "aafafe3c-b8e9-476c-fbe2-41c0dbb247d3"
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "display_data",
          "data": {
            "text/plain": [
              "<Figure size 640x480 with 1 Axes>"
            ],
            "image/png": "\n"
          },
          "metadata": {}
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "fig, ax = plt.subplots()\n",
        "sns.regplot(x=\"cars_per_1000\", y=\"emission_pc\", data=no_lu, ax=ax)\n",
        "ax.set_xlabel(\"Cars per 1000 inhabitants\")\n",
        "ax.set_ylabel(\"Tonnes per inhabitant\")\n",
        "ax.set_title(\"Cars and emissions\")\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ]
    },
    {
