      "source": [
        "coefficients = pd.DataFrame()\n",
        "coefficients[\"Model 1\"] = model_cars.params\n",
        "coefficients[\"p-value 1\"] = model_cars.pvalues\n",
        "coefficients[\"Model 2\"] = model_emission.params\n",
        "coefficients[\"p-value 2\"] = model_emission.pvalues\n",
        "\n",
        "coefficients.round(8)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "ca6a5252",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "ca6a5252"
      },
      "source": [
        "## 10. The five assumptions\n",
        "\n",
        "We test both models."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "45bbf4be",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "45bbf4be"
      },
      "source": [
        "### 10.1 Linearity\n",
        "\n",
        "The residuals should lie around zero without a pattern. A curve or a funnel\n",
        "would mean the wrong form."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "c4b22d62",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "c4b22d62"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "fig, ax = plt.subplots()\n",
        "ax.scatter(model_cars.fittedvalues, model_cars.resid)\n",
        "ax.set_xlabel(\"Fitted values\")\n",
        "ax.set_ylabel(\"Residuals\")\n",
        "ax.set_title(\"Model 1\")\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "50034474",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "50034474"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "fig, ax = plt.subplots()\n",
        "ax.scatter(model_emission.fittedvalues, model_emission.resid)\n",
        "ax.set_xlabel(\"Fitted values\")\n",
        "ax.set_ylabel(\"Residuals\")\n",
        "ax.set_title(\"Model 2\")\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "070c4199",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "070c4199"
      },
      "source": [
        "### 10.2 Multicollinearity\n",
        "\n",
        "A VIF above 10 is a problem."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "9b10de52",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "9b10de52"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "vif_cars = pd.DataFrame()\n",
        "vif_cars[\"Variable\"] = x_cars.columns\n",
        "\n",
        "values = []\n",
        "for i in range(x_cars.shape[1]):\n",
        "    values.append(variance_inflation_factor(x_cars.values, i))\n",
        "vif_cars[\"VIF\"] = values\n",
        "\n",
        "vif_cars.round(2)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "8a7c600e",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "8a7c600e"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "vif_emission = pd.DataFrame()\n",
        "vif_emission[\"Variable\"] = x_emission.columns\n",
        "\n",
        "values = []\n",
        "for i in range(x_emission.shape[1]):\n",
        "    values.append(variance_inflation_factor(x_emission.values, i))\n",
        "vif_emission[\"VIF\"] = values\n",
        "\n",
        "vif_emission.round(2)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "2f894c5a",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "2f894c5a"
      },
      "source": [
        "A high VIF for `gdp_pc` and `gdp_pc2` in model 1 is normal. A variable and\n",
        "its own square are always strongly correlated. This is not a mistake, it only\n",
        "makes the two single coefficients harder to read."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "69a98f4c",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "69a98f4c"
      },
      "source": [
        "### 10.3 Homoscedasticity\n",
        "\n",
        "Breusch-Pagan. A p-value above 0.05 means the variance is constant enough."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "a02ba711",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "a02ba711"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "bp_cars = smd.het_breuschpagan(model_cars.resid, x_cars)\n",
        "bp_emission = smd.het_breuschpagan(model_emission.resid, x_emission)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Model 1 p-value:\", round(bp_cars[1], 4))\n",
        "print(\"Model 2 p-value:\", round(bp_emission[1], 4))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "dd1016dd",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "dd1016dd"
      },
      "source": [
        "### 10.4 Autocorrelation\n",
        "\n",
        "Durbin-Watson. A value around 2 is fine. Countries have no natural order, so\n",
        "this test says little here."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "62510f47",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "62510f47"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "print(\"Model 1:\", round(durbin_watson(model_cars.resid), 3))\n",
        "print(\"Model 2:\", round(durbin_watson(model_emission.resid), 3))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "6eeb6b8f",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "6eeb6b8f"
      },
      "source": [
        "### 10.5 Normal residuals\n",
        "\n",
        "The histogram should look like a bell. In the Q-Q plot the points should follow\n",
        "the line."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "c2a6a584",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "c2a6a584"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "fig, ax = plt.subplots()\n",
        "sns.histplot(model_cars.resid, kde=True, ax=ax)\n",
        "ax.set_xlabel(\"Residual\")\n",
        "ax.set_title(\"Model 1\")\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "6507e557",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "6507e557"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "sm.qqplot(model_cars.resid, line=\"s\")\n",
        "plt.title(\"Model 1\")\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "380edd82",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "380edd82"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "fig, ax = plt.subplots()\n",
        "sns.histplot(model_emission.resid, kde=True, ax=ax)\n",
        "ax.set_xlabel(\"Residual\")\n",
        "ax.set_title(\"Model 2\")\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "9de1d898",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "9de1d898"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "sm.qqplot(model_emission.resid, line=\"s\")\n",
        "plt.title(\"Model 2\")\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "5d3d7ef9",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "5d3d7ef9"
      },
      "source": [
        "Shapiro-Wilk. A p-value above 0.05 means the residuals are normal enough."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 45,
      "id": "75c591a0",
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "75c591a0",
        "outputId": "829c08fe-1693-4224-f86b-b97fe4b5a86a"
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "Model 1 p-value: 0.3642\n",
            "Model 2 p-value: 0.9894\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "shapiro_cars = stats.shapiro(model_cars.resid)\n",
        "shapiro_emission = stats.shapiro(model_emission.resid)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Model 1 p-value:\", round(shapiro_cars[1], 4))\n",
        "print(\"Model 2 p-value:\", round(shapiro_emission[1], 4))"
      ]
    }
  ],
